        "approval_date": "4th July 2025",
        "version": null,
        "text": "Costs\n(9)\nAll costs associated with applications for all Visa’s are the responsibility of the School/Division and/or the individual (where required)."
    },
    {
        "chunk_id": "98-11",
        "document_id": "98",
        "policy_title": "Visa Sponsorship Policy",
        "heading_level": "h4",
        "section": "Section 5 - Policy Statement",
        "subsection": null,
        "topic": null,
        "subtopic": "Visa Application Requirements",
        "paragraph_start": 10,
        "paragraph_end": 11,
        "source_url": "https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/view.php?id=98",
        "status_details_url": "https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/status-and-details.php?id=98",
        "status": "Current",
        "effective_date": "4th July 2025",
        "review_date": "4th July 2028",
        "approval_authority": "Vice-Chancellor",
        "approval_date": "4th July 2025",
        "version": null,
        "text": "Visa Application Requirements\n(10)\nVisa requirements are determined by the\nDepartment of Home Affairs (DHA)\n. The University’s Immigration Lawyer will guide the individual on requirements.\n(11)\nConditions of La Trobe Sponsorship\nin accordance with Australian legislation, staff cannot commence employment until they have been granted the appropriate visa by DHA;\nindividuals cannot commence relocation (where funded by the University) until they have been granted the appropriate visa by DHA;\nindividuals who self-fund relocation to Australia may commence relocation arrangements however should the visa not be granted, the University will not be responsible for any reimbursement of costs;\nindividuals must comply with the rules of their visa;\nthe University will abide by all obligations of the relevant visa of an individual;\nstaff cannot work beyond their visa expiry date, unless an extension is applied for and granted;\njob offers are subject to visa approval; refer ‘Visa Not Granted by Government’ below;\nrepatriation costs are not automatically included in the sponsorship. Staff may discuss their requirements with their hiring manager. The University will however comply with any legislated requirements that may be relevant at the time of repatriation."
    },
    {
        "chunk_id": "98-12",
        "document_id": "98",
        "policy_title": "Visa Sponsorship Policy",
        "heading_level": "h4",
        "section": "Section 5 - Policy Statement",
        "subsection": null,
        "topic": null,
        "subtopic": "Visa Not Granted by DHA",
        "paragraph_start": 12,
        "paragraph_end": 12,
        "source_url": "https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/view.php?id=98",
        "status_details_url": "https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/status-and-details.php?id=98",
        "status": "Current",
        "effective_date": "4th July 2025",
        "review_date": "4th July 2028",
        "approval_authority": "Vice-Chancellor",
        "approval_date": "4th July 2025",
        "version": null,
        "text": "Visa Not Granted by DHA\n(12)\nIf a visa is not granted by DHA, any offer or contract of employment will become null and void."
    },
    {
        "chunk_id": "98-13",
        "document_id": "98",
        "policy_title": "Visa Sponsorship Policy",
        "heading_level": "h4",
        "section": "Section 5 - Policy Statement",
        "subsection": null,
        "topic": null,
        "subtopic": "Termination of Employment",
        "paragraph_start": 13,
        "paragraph_end": 13,
        "source_url": "https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/view.php?id=98",
        "status_details_url": "https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/status-and-details.php?id=98",
        "status": "Current",
        "effective_date": "4th July 2025",
        "review_date": "4th July 2028",
        "approval_authority": "Vice-Chancellor",
        "approval_date": "4th July 2025",
        "version": null,
        "text": "Termination of Employment\n(13)\nBoth the individual and the University must comply with their legislated requirements where a termination of employment has occurred."
    },
    {
        "chunk_id": "98-14",
        "document_id": "98",
        "policy_title": "Visa Sponsorship Policy",
        "heading_level": "h3",
        "section": "Section 6 - Procedures",
        "subsection": null,
        "topic": "Applications",
        "subtopic": null,
        "paragraph_start": 14,
        "paragraph_end": 20,
        "source_url": "https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/view.php?id=98",
        "status_details_url": "https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/status-and-details.php?id=98",
        "status": "Current",
        "effective_date": "4th July 2025",
        "review_date": "4th July 2028",
        "approval_authority": "Vice-Chancellor",
        "approval_date": "4th July 2025",
        "version": null,
        "text": "Applications\n(14)\nA preferred candidate is identified and working rights for Australia are confirmed.\n(15)\nShould a visa sponsorship/permanent residency be required, relevant approvals are obtained.\n(16)\nPeople & Culture engages the Immigration Lawyer to manage the relevant visa requirements and application.\n(17)\nPeople & Culture collates the required documentation from the individual and forward this to the Immigration Lawyer.\n(18)\nThe Immigration Lawyer will coordinate the application liaising directly with the individual.\n(19)\nPeople & Culture, with relevant approvals, proceeds to appoint the individual to the position subject to the visa application outcome.\n(20)\nThe Immigration Lawyer will notify both the individual and La Trobe of the outcome of the application."
    },
    {
        "chunk_id": "98-15",
        "document_id": "98",
        "policy_title": "Visa Sponsorship Policy",
        "heading_level": "h3",
        "section": "Section 6 - Procedures",
        "subsection": null,
        "topic": "Renewal",
        "subtopic": null,
        "paragraph_start": 21,
        "paragraph_end": 21,
        "source_url": "https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/view.php?id=98",
        "status_details_url": "https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/status-and-details.php?id=98",
        "status": "Current",
        "effective_date": "4th July 2025",
        "review_date": "4th July 2028",
        "approval_authority": "Vice-Chancellor",
        "approval_date": "4th July 2025",
        "version": null,
        "text": "Renewal\n(21)\nVisas identified as requiring renewal are notified via the University’s HRIS to the Hiring Manager and the individual."
    },
    {
        "chunk_id": "98-16",
        "document_id": "98",
        "policy_title": "Visa Sponsorship Policy",
        "heading_level": "h3",
        "section": "Section 6 - Procedures",
        "subsection": null,
        "topic": "Responsibilities",
        "subtopic": null,
        "paragraph_start": 22,
        "paragraph_end": 24,
        "source_url": "https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/view.php?id=98",
        "status_details_url": "https://policies.latrobe.edu.au/document/status-and-details.php?id=98",
        "status": "Current",
        "effective_date": "4th July 2025",
        "review_date": "4th July 2028",
        "approval_authority": "Vice-Chancellor",
        "approval_date": "4th July 2025",
        "version": null,
        "text": "Responsibilities\n(22)\nPeople & Culture is responsible for:\nconfirming visa requirements with the Immigration Lawyer;\nliaising with the Immigration Lawyer to facilitate visa applications; and\nnotifying the hiring manager and all relevant stakeholders of the visa application outcome.\n(23)\nImmigration Lawyer is responisble for:\nadvising the Talent Acquisition team member and staff member/area on what visa is appropriate for the proposed appointment;\nlodging visa applications with DHA ensuring compliance with the sponsorship requirements;\nproviding immigration assistance to current and prospective staff members; and\nnotifying the Talent Acquisition team member of documentation required and the progress of the application.\n(24)\nThe individual is responsible for:\nnotifying the University of any conditions associated with a current VISA or if they have a VISA sponsored by another employer;\nensuring their current VISA is valid and they must notify People & Culture of any renewal or VISA status changes for our records and compliance."
    },
    {
